---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import CTAFooter from "../components/CTAFooter.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service — Vera AI"
  description="Terms of Service for Vera AI, a product of Arsent LLC. Subscription, billing, refund, cancellation, acceptable use, and liability terms."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="terms">
    <div class="terms-inner">
      <header class="terms-header">
        <div class="terms-badge">Terms of Service</div>
        <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="terms-subtitle">
          Vera is a product of <strong>Arsent LLC</strong>, a Delaware limited
          liability company based in San Francisco, CA. These Terms govern
          your access to and use of Vera.
        </p>
        <p class="last-updated">Last updated: April 7, 2026</p>
      </header>

      <section class="callout">
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <ul class="callout-list">
          <li>
            Vera is a subscription SaaS product. The Pro plan is
            <strong>$50 USD/month</strong> or
            <strong>$500 USD/year</strong>, with a <strong>3-day free
            trial</strong> for new workspaces.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Cancel anytime</strong> from your billing dashboard. Your
            subscription stays active through the end of your current billing
            period and is not renewed.
          </li>
          <li>
            We do <strong>not pro-rate refunds</strong> for partial periods,
            but we will review billing errors and extended outages on a
            case-by-case basis.
          </li>
          <li>
            You own your code and data. We don't train models on your data
            and we don't sell it. See the
            <a href="/privacy" class="inline-link">privacy notice</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            For legal questions email
            <a href="mailto:legal@agent-vera.com">legal@agent-vera.com</a>.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          Vera ("Vera", "the Service") is operated by Arsent LLC ("Arsent",
          "we", "us", "our"), a Delaware limited liability company based in
          San Francisco, California, United States.
        </p>
        <p>
          By creating an account, installing Vera into your Slack workspace,
          or otherwise accessing the Service, you ("Customer", "you") agree
          to be bound by these Terms of Service ("Terms"). If you are
          accepting these Terms on behalf of an organization, you represent
          that you have authority to bind that organization, and "you" refers
          to that organization.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>2. Account and access</h2>
        <p>
          To use Vera, you must create a workspace by installing the Vera
          Slack application and authorizing the requested OAuth scopes for
          Slack, Linear, and GitHub as needed. You are responsible for
          maintaining the confidentiality of your account credentials and
          for all activity that occurs under your workspace.
        </p>
        <p>
          You must be at least 18 years old and legally able to enter into
          contracts to use Vera. Vera is intended for business use; we do not
          knowingly accept consumer accounts.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>3. Subscription, free trial, and billing</h2>
        <h3 class="sub-heading">Plans and prices</h3>
        <p>
          Vera is offered on a subscription basis at the following prices,
          all in US dollars (USD):
        </p>
        <ul class="rights-list">
          <li><strong>Pro Monthly</strong> — $50 USD per workspace per month</li>
          <li><strong>Pro Yearly</strong> — $500 USD per workspace per year</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Each plan includes a monthly allowance of LLM token usage that
          covers normal team workloads. Usage above the allowance is billed
          as metered overage at the rates published in your account
          dashboard. We will notify you in-product before applying any
          overage charge.
        </p>

        <h3 class="sub-heading">Free trial</h3>
        <p>
          New workspaces receive a <strong>3-day free trial</strong> of the
          Pro plan with no payment method required to begin. To continue
          using Vera past the end of the trial, add a payment method and
          select a plan from your billing dashboard.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you do not add a payment method before the trial ends, your
          workspace is paused. Paused workspace data is retained for 30 days
          and then deleted.
        </p>

        <h3 class="sub-heading">Billing and renewals</h3>
        <p>
          Subscriptions automatically renew at the end of each billing
          period (monthly or yearly) at the then-current price for your
          plan, until you cancel. We use <strong>Stripe</strong> as our
          payment processor — your card details are handled directly by
          Stripe and are not stored on our servers.
        </p>
        <p>
          Failed payments may result in your subscription being marked
          past-due and your workspace being temporarily suspended. We will
          email you and prompt you in-product to update your payment method.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>4. Cancellation and refunds</h2>
        <h3 class="sub-heading">Cancellation</h3>
        <p>
          You can cancel your subscription at any time from the
          <a href="/account/billing" class="inline-link">billing dashboard</a>
          or by emailing
          <a href="mailto:billing@agent-vera.com">billing@agent-vera.com</a>.
          When you cancel, your subscription remains active through the end
          of your current billing period and is not renewed. You will retain
          access to Vera until the period ends.
        </p>

        <h3 class="sub-heading">Refunds</h3>
        <p>
          All fees are non-refundable. We do not pro-rate refunds for
          partial billing periods, unused features, or downgraded plans.
        </p>
        <p>
          We will, however, review the following on a case-by-case basis and
          may issue a refund or credit at our discretion:
        </p>
        <ul class="rights-list">
          <li><strong>Billing errors</strong> — duplicate charges, wrong amounts, charges after cancellation</li>
          <li><strong>Extended service unavailability</strong> — material outages preventing normal use of Vera</li>
          <li><strong>Required by law</strong> — refunds required by applicable consumer protection law</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To request a refund review, email
          <a href="mailto:billing@agent-vera.com">billing@agent-vera.com</a>
          with your workspace name and the charge in question.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>
          You agree not to use Vera to:
        </p>
        <ul class="rights-list">
          <li>Violate any law or third-party right, including intellectual property and privacy rights</li>
          <li>Generate, store, or distribute malware, exploit code intended for unauthorized access, or content prohibited by our model providers</li>
          <li>Send spam, conduct phishing, or otherwise harm third parties</li>
          <li>Reverse engineer, decompile, or attempt to extract the source code of Vera or its underlying models</li>
          <li>Resell, sublicense, or provide Vera as a service to third parties without written permission</li>
          <li>Interfere with or disrupt the integrity or performance of the Service or its infrastructure</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We may suspend or terminate accounts that violate this section,
          with or without notice depending on severity.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>6. Customer data and intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          You retain all right, title, and interest in and to your code,
          prompts, and any output Vera generates for you ("Customer Data").
          We claim no ownership over Customer Data.
        </p>
        <p>
          You grant Arsent a limited, non-exclusive license to process
          Customer Data solely as needed to provide Vera, including
          transmitting prompts to model providers, storing logs for
          debugging and recovery, and operating the service generally. We
          do not use Customer Data to train or fine-tune any model. See the
          <a href="/privacy" class="inline-link">privacy notice</a> for full
          detail on what we collect and how long we keep it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Vera, the Vera and Arsent names and logos, and all related
          software, design, and documentation are owned by Arsent LLC and
          its licensors and are protected by intellectual property laws.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>7. Service availability and changes</h2>
        <p>
          We work hard to keep Vera available, but we do not guarantee
          uninterrupted access. The Service may be temporarily unavailable
          due to scheduled maintenance, infrastructure issues, third-party
          outages (Anthropic, Slack, GitHub, Linear, Cloudflare, Fly.io),
          or events beyond our reasonable control.
        </p>
        <p>
          We may add, modify, or remove features from Vera at any time. If a
          change materially reduces the functionality of a plan you are
          subscribed to, we will notify you and offer you a pro-rated refund
          if you choose to cancel as a result.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>8. Disclaimers</h2>
        <p>
          Vera generates code and other outputs using large language models.
          These outputs may be incorrect, incomplete, or unsuitable for your
          purpose. <strong>You are responsible for reviewing all output
          before relying on it</strong>, including running tests, performing
          code review, and validating that any pull request Vera opens meets
          your standards before merging.
        </p>
        <p>
          THE SERVICE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE", WITHOUT
          WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING WARRANTIES
          OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND
          NON-INFRINGEMENT. We do not warrant that Vera will be error-free
          or that defects will be corrected.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>9. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, ARSENT LLC SHALL NOT BE
          LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR
          PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR ANY LOSS OF PROFITS, REVENUE, DATA, OR
          BUSINESS OPPORTUNITY, ARISING OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH YOUR
          USE OF VERA, EVEN IF WE HAVE BEEN ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF
          SUCH DAMAGES.
        </p>
        <p>
          OUR TOTAL LIABILITY FOR ANY CLAIM ARISING OUT OF OR RELATING TO
          THESE TERMS OR THE SERVICE IS LIMITED TO THE GREATER OF
          (A) ONE HUNDRED US DOLLARS ($100) OR (B) THE FEES YOU PAID TO US
          FOR THE SERVICE IN THE TWELVE MONTHS PRECEDING THE CLAIM.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>10. Indemnification</h2>
        <p>
          You agree to defend, indemnify, and hold harmless Arsent LLC and
          its officers, employees, and agents from any claims, damages, or
          expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees) arising out of
          your use of Vera, your violation of these Terms, or your
          violation of any third-party right.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>11. Termination</h2>
        <p>
          You may stop using Vera and cancel your subscription at any time
          as described in Section 4. We may suspend or terminate your access
          to Vera at any time, with or without notice, if you violate these
          Terms or if we are required to do so by law.
        </p>
        <p>
          On termination, your right to access Vera ends immediately. We
          will retain your data for the periods described in our
          <a href="/privacy" class="inline-link">privacy notice</a> and then
          delete it. Sections that by their nature should survive
          termination (including ownership, disclaimers, limitation of
          liability, indemnification, and governing law) will survive.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>12. Governing law and disputes</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of Delaware,
          without regard to conflict-of-laws principles. Any dispute arising
          out of or relating to these Terms or the Service shall be brought
          exclusively in the state or federal courts located in San
          Francisco County, California, and you consent to the personal
          jurisdiction of those courts.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>13. Changes to these Terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these Terms from time to time. Material changes
          will be communicated by email or in-product notice. Your continued
          use of Vera after the effective date of revised Terms constitutes
          acceptance of the changes. The <strong>Last updated</strong> date
          at the top of this page reflects the most recent revision.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="contact">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For legal questions or notices, email
          <a href="mailto:legal@agent-vera.com">legal@agent-vera.com</a>.
          For billing questions, email
          <a href="mailto:billing@agent-vera.com">billing@agent-vera.com</a>.
          For general support, email
          <a href="mailto:support@agent-vera.com">support@agent-vera.com</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Arsent LLC is based in San Francisco, California, United States.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <CTAFooter />
</Layout>

<style>
  .terms {
    padding: 8rem 1.5rem 4rem;
  }

  .terms-inner {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .terms-header {
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .terms-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.35rem 1rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(13, 40, 24, 0.3);
    border-radius: 100px;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .terms-subtitle {
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2vw, 1.2rem);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 650px;
  }

  .terms-subtitle strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .last-updated {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    opacity: 0.7;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .callout {
    padding: 2.5rem;
    border: 2px solid rgba(13, 40, 24, 0.2);
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4);
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .callout h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .callout-list {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .callout-list li {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .callout-list li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.6em;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-text);
  }

  .callout-list strong,
  .callout-list a {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .callout-list a {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .section {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .section h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .section > p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .section > p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .section .sub-heading {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .section a {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .inline-link {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .rights-list {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin: 1rem 0;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .rights-list li {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    position: relative;
  }

  .rights-list li::before {
    content: "→";
    position: absolute;
    left: -1.5rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    opacity: 0.5;
  }

  .rights-list strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .contact {
    padding: 2.5rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(13, 40, 24, 0.12);
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.3);
  }

  .contact h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .contact p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .contact p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .contact a {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .terms {
      padding: 4rem 1.5rem 2rem;
    }
  }
</style>
